INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES
  ('new-safety-standards-for-california''s-workers-as-heatwaves-intensify', 'New Safety Standards for California''s Workers as Heatwaves Intensify', 'Keeping Workers Safe in Rising Temperatures.', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Keeping Workers Safe in Rising Temperatures."},{"type":"p","text":"Following the state''s first dangerous heatwave of 2024, California has implemented new standards set to protect restaurant kitchen staff and other workers who labor indoors in what can be, at times, blistering conditions. Announced Thursday, the new regulations will require businesses to take protective measures when indoor temperatures hit more than 87 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"type":"p","text":"Changes in Regulations for Indoor Workplaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Under new proposed changes, businesses must ensure that workplaces are not cooled to no more than 87 degrees \"if feasible.\" For those workers in protective clothing and who deal with high-heat-producing machinery like stoves and ovens, the maximum limit will be pegged at below 82 degrees. Other measures include employers being required to provide access to water, \"cool-down areas,\" and rest breaks to help mitigate the effects of excessive heat."},{"type":"p","text":"Details of the New Standards"},{"type":"p","text":"The state Occupational Safety and Health Standards Board, the same board that unveiled those changes, did not speak to what circumstances might render cooling measures infeasible, though the regulations do single out restaurant kitchens as being uniquely indoors and in need of such additional protections."},{"type":"p","text":"Process for Approval and Implementation"},{"type":"p","text":"The revised employer requirements should be submitted for the review of regulatory changes to the state''s Office of Administrative Law within 30 business days for approval or rejection. The OSHSB asked that the requirements be operative immediately upon approval by the Administrative Law Office."},{"type":"p","text":"Heatwave Warnings and Broader Impact"},{"type":"p","text":"These regulatory updates come at a time when meteorologists have warned about triple-digit temperatures in parts of California. Last weekend, a record-breaking area stretching as far as Vermont was similarly scorching."},{"type":"p","text":"Growing Attention to Heat Safety on the Job"},{"type":"p","text":"Dangerous heat in the workplace has grown as a point of increasing focus by safety officials and organized labor as temperatures smash records. Preliminary data for 2023 tallies 2,030 heat-related deaths in the United States, the highest count in the last 45 years such data has been tracked. That is a significant rise from 1,600 fatalities in 2021 and 1,722 in 2022, according to the U.S. Health & Human Services Department. This includes all heat-related deaths, not only those at workplaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Federal Efforts to Combat Workplace Heat"},{"type":"p","text":"Nearly three years ago the White House ordered the U.S. Department of Labor to revise federal Occupational Safety & Health Administration, or OSHA, standards to better protect workers from excessive heat. To that end, a proposed set of federal safeguards is under review by the White House Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs."},{"type":"p","text":"Recap of proposed new heat standards"},{"type":"p","text":"California has enacted new regulations requiring employers to protect indoor workers, particularly restaurant kitchen staff and others who work in extremely hot conditions. Employers must now take protective action when indoor temperatures rise higher than 87 degrees. This includes: cooling the workspace to no more than 87 degrees when feasible; or, to as low as 82 degrees when employees must wear protective clothing or work near radiant heat sources. In addition, employers are mandated to provide access to water, cool-down areas, and rest breaks."},{"type":"p","text":"Information on Feasibility and Affected Workplaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Although the OSHSB did not elaborate on any conditions under which cooling measures would be deemed infeasible, restaurant kitchens have been especially singled out as one of the kinds of workplaces to be positively impacted by this regulation."},{"type":"p","text":"Timeline for Review and Approval"},{"type":"p","text":"The Office of Administrative Law has 30 business days to review the new standards. The OSHSB has requested that the measures be put into effect immediately upon approval."},{"type":"p","text":"Broader Heatwave Impact and Safety Focus"},{"type":"p","text":"With meteorologists predicting triple-digit temperatures in parts of California, and much of the country baking last weekend, an already heightened focus takes place on workplace heat safety. The record heat brought increased scrutiny from safety officials and labor organizations."},{"type":"p","text":"Alarming Statistics on Heat-Related Fatalities"},{"type":"p","text":"In 2022, the United States broke a record with 2,030 heat-related illness deaths, the highest in 45 years. There were 1,600 deaths in 2021, while this year the death count rose to 1,722, prompting alarm over an ominous trend of extreme heat."},{"type":"p","text":"Federal Action on Heat Safety Standards"},{"type":"p","text":"Amid escalating heat dangers, nearly three years ago, the White House ordered the U.S. Department of Labor to update OSHA standards. Proposed federal protections were submitted to the White House Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs for review."},{"type":"p","text":"To Sum Up"},{"type":"p","text":"California''s new standards for the protection of indoor workers from excessive heat reflect a growing awareness of the dangers posed by extreme temperatures. At the same time, as the state waits to see these regulations approved and implemented, this broad effort of improvement in workplace safety in the face of rising temperatures remains a critical issue nationwide."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_1a765c95a613400382b74b72c6dbbdb3~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(21).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-28', 'published'),
  ('dubai''s-krasota-restaurant-revives-legendary-chef-with-ai-for-a-unique-dining-experience', 'Dubai''s Krasota Restaurant Revives Legendary Chef with AI for a Unique Dining Experience', 'The Future of Food: Dubai''s AI-Powered Restaurant', '[{"type":"h2","text":"The Future of Food: Dubai''s AI-Powered Restaurant"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in the fine dining area of Dubai, Krasota epitomizes how frontier technologies like Artificial Intelligence are extending the horizons of culinary innovation; the great restaurant features multisensory dining in store and is continuously inviting foodies from around the world for treatment. The way this fine dining restaurant has described the dishes as \"bringing the late French chef Paul Bocuse back to life\" has charmed its patrons."},{"type":"p","text":"Krasota, which offers an eight-course \"Imaginary Futures\" show, was co-founded by entrepreneur Boris Zarkov, renowned chef Vladimir Mukhin, and digital artist Anton Nenashev. Guests are taken through futuristic visions during this experience. Every course has a carefully chosen theme, which might be anything from space colonies to underwater cities, according to CNN."},{"type":"p","text":"Deepfake Technology and AI"},{"type":"p","text":"Krasota''s creative method is centered on its use of deepfake and AI technology to produce lifelike videos of the late, great chef Paul Bocuse, who passed away in 2018. In these videos, Bocuse talks about and explains the finer points of the food that is served. Deepfake algorithms and AI-generated projections are the technologies underlying this. The technologies are remarkably accurate in recreating the voice and likeness of Bocuse."},{"type":"p","text":"Nenashev used 3D computer graphics software to design the projections. On the other hand, Mukhin reinvented some of Bocuse''s most well-known dishes, like his truffle V.G.E soup, using the generative platform Midjourney. The end effect is a sense of the digital age that brings back memories and style of Bocuse. For the customers, dining here offers an alternative form of amusement and education."},{"type":"p","text":"Using Deepfake Videos Into The Dining"},{"type":"p","text":"The dining experience at Krasota incorporates the deepfake videos. A 20-seat circular table is surrounded by curved walls that act as projection screens in this dimly lit, round dining area. 3D video graphics are displayed on more than 20 projectors. These give life to the deepfake Bocuse. Then, with thorough explanations, the late chef leads the diners through each course."},{"type":"p","text":"This immersive setup is further enhanced by an artificial intelligence-powered interactive tabletop that has sensors to distinguish between different objects. Targeted projections, like fireflies on glasses and plates, are the result. In space-themed scenarios, there are interactive gaming elements as well, such as shooting passing spaceships."},{"type":"p","text":"According to Zarkov, there are several reasons to use deepfake and AI technology. Improving the dining experience''s educational and entertainment value is the main objective. Through the modernization of Bocuse''s culinary legacy, Krasota establishes a personal connection between the chef and the patrons. The restaurant honors his contributions to fine dining in this way."},{"type":"p","text":"In summary, Krasota is a shining example of culinary innovation in Dubai''s dynamic dining scene, where technology and the art of cooking coexist harmoniously. By leveraging artificial intelligence and deepfake technology, Krasota can bring diners into a multi-sensory experience that transports them to hypothetical futures while also bringing back the renowned Chef Paul Bocuse, who used his remarkable realism to explain and explain each dish. Krasota is a restaurant that was co-founded by industry pioneers Anton Nenashev, Vladimir Mukhin, and Boris Zarkov. It shows how artificial intelligence (AI) can go beyond traditional dining experiences by providing customers with more than just a meal; instead, it offers them an interactive exploration of culinary history and future possibilities."},{"type":"p","text":"By fusing state-of-the-art technology with exquisite culinary artistry, Krasota creates a lasting tribute to Chef Bocuse''s legacy while also providing entertainment and education. In addition to entertaining and educating guests, Krasota pays a heartfelt tribute to Chef Bocuse''s enduring legacy by Fusing state-of-the-art technology with exquisite culinary craftsmanship, imparting connections to the past with the most exquisite dining experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_c301d5990dc648c98428ddd39cc1242c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_3000,h_2000,al_c,q_90/dubai.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-27', 'published'),
  ('voice-ai-advancements:-soundhound-expands-restaurant-ordering', 'Voice AI Advancements: SoundHound Expands Restaurant Ordering', 'Transforming Dining Experiences with Advanced Voice AI Integration', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Transforming Dining Experiences with Advanced Voice AI Integration"},{"type":"p","text":"SoundHound AI announced Tuesday (June 18) the acquisition of key assets from Allset, an online food ordering platform, in another step toward further entrenching the voice artificial intelligence company within the restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"SoundHound AI Acquires Allset Restaurant Network"},{"type":"p","text":"The transaction, the financial terms of which were not disclosed, brings almost 7,000 restaurant partners of Allset and engineering talent under the SoundHound umbrella. It also turns up the dial on further accelerating the development of voice ordering solutions for food service on cars, TVs, and other smart devices."},{"type":"p","text":"Advancing Voice AI in Food Service"},{"type":"p","text":"It''s an AI-powered speech technology-growing sector. As PYMNTS recently reported, McDonald''s ended its partnership with IBM to develop an AI-powered drive-thru system, deciding to pull the tech from more than 100 restaurants. A lot of what the fast-food chain has done underscores that challenges and opportunities are trailing behind the adoption of AI voice-ordering systems at a time when there is a general lack of labor and pressure on the industry for streamlined operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Voice AI is seen by SoundHound, which already works with over 10,000 restaurant locations, as a game-changing technology for the food service sector. Its systems allow for customer orders, support multiple languages, and are integrated directly with point-of-sale systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Challenges and Opportunities in AI-Powered Ordering"},{"type":"p","text":"Keyvan Mohajer, CEO and co-founder of SoundHound AI stated in the news release that \"combining forces, we will continue to deliver dynamic and convenient ways for people to order food items and complete a vast array of everyday transactions, just by talking naturally.\""},{"type":"p","text":"SoundHound''s Vision for Voice-Enabled Transactions"},{"type":"p","text":"The acquisition comes as restaurants get increasing recourse to technology to streamline operations and cut rising costs. The voice AI systems promise improved efficiency with automated order-taking and freeing of staff for other tasks."},{"type":"p","text":"Impact on Restaurant Operations and Costs"},{"type":"p","text":"Founded in 2015, Allset built its business around providing a platform for local food pickup that allowed restaurants and consumers to bypass exorbitant fees associated with delivery apps. The investment-backed company, with investors like Andreessen Horowitz, will bring its marketplace experience into SoundHound."},{"type":"p","text":"Allset''s Marketplace Expertise Joins SoundHound"},{"type":"p","text":"Stas Matviyenko, the co-founder and CEO of Allset, will bring his team to SoundHound. The news release said, \"We realized right away that we share the same vision for the voice commerce ecosystem that elevates the consumer experience.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Future Outlook: Voice Commerce in the Restaurant Industry"},{"type":"p","text":"Such integration of Allset''s restaurant relationships with the prowess of SoundHound voice AI could go on to fast-track mainstream adoption in voice ordering across a wide gamut of platforms. That ties well into the bigger picture, too, where tech giants and start-ups are racing to integrate voice assistants in a gamut of everyday consumer interactions."},{"type":"p","text":"With voice recognition technology improving day by day, voice commerce is expected to grow manifold in the next few years. SoundHound is increasing its investments in the Allset acquisition, this is one strategic move to help voice commerce grow with such a steep trend and be at the top among competitors in the Voice AI marketplace."},{"type":"p","text":"The acquisition of key assets from Allset by SoundHound AI becomes a gigantic step to enhance its capabilities in voice artificial intelligence in restaurants. This strategic acquisition brings almost 7,000 restaurant partners and engineering talent, further benefiting SoundHound on its commitment to changing food service through innovative technology."},{"type":"p","text":"Through this integration, Allset''s marketplace experience will combine with SoundHound''s leading-edge voice AI technology to bring much-needed dynamic enhancements across multiple platforms in customer interaction and operational efficiency. With industries turning toward automation and digital transformation, voice AI systems will help in easily taking orders and offsetting overload operationally during these constrained times of labor."},{"type":"p","text":"That development envisaged the broad challenges and potential of AI in restaurant operation optimization. With additional functionality, SoundHound can power such applications with natively seamless, multilingual voice interactions at the point of sale to drive further convenience and customer satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"Looking forward, given the potential rise of voice recognition technology, SoundHound wants to further grow voice commerce. With this acquisition, the company will be at the forefront of leading and prepared to play a major role in the transformation of consumer engagement with food service providers through smart, intuitive, and voice-controlled solutions."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_863093fb1b074d13a41f52a04040a2c0~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/102(27-june-news-blog-image).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-26', 'published'),
  ('freedompay-and-toast-survey-reveals-key-focus:-data-security,-integration,-and-growth', 'FreedomPay and Toast Survey Reveals Key Focus: Data Security, Integration, and Growth', 'Enterprise Hospitality Insights: Data Security, Integration & Growth', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Enterprise Hospitality Insights: Data Security, Integration & Growth"},{"type":"p","text":"A recent study by FreedomPay, the global leader in Next Level CommerceTM solutions aligned with Toast, the leading cloud-based restaurant management software company, to bring important insights on what matters most to enterprise hospitality leaders. Key among these findings is the fact that data security, system integration, and enablement of growth are major critical vectors in the making of both merchant preference and trust within payment solutions and point-of-sale providers."},{"type":"p","text":"Key Takeaways from the Survey"},{"type":"p","text":"The survey gives crystal-clear insight into what enterprise hospitality leaders value most when selecting payment solutions and Point-of-sale systems. Notably, 53% of the overall population of merchants expressed a need for help in prioritizing their technology spend, which makes a strong business case for integrated solutions that can deliver full value and make informed decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"Data Security: An Issue of Paramount Importance"},{"type":"p","text":"The central finding that has emerged from the survey is that merchants unanimously agree on the issue of data security. All the participants believed that data security was important, although only 98% of them stated that data privacy is a major consideration in selecting a payment solution. In an era characterized by increased cyber threats, rigorous measures on security have never been needed more than now. Those providers that provide quality security protocols and adhere to standards, as validated by the PCI Security Standards Council in FreedomPay, will engender trust from a greater number of merchants."},{"type":"p","text":"Integration: The Basis of Operational Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"System integration as another critical factor comes out to be an area where most merchants would be looking to have a rather highly integrated system. The results of the survey suggest that 85% of merchants have their payment systems either fully integrated or integrated to a very high level with other software. Seamless integration means easy operations, accuracy of data, and a view of business performance in its entirety for informed decisions. This simplifies operations, reduces errors, and increases efficiency, generally making integrated solutions quite impossible to eliminate from modern hospitality businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"Customer Support and User Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Good customer support was nominated by 49%, 46% said ease of use, and 44% said reliability. This shows that maybe the systems need to be reliable, accessible, and user-friendly. On the other hand, such responsive support services and easy interfaces considerably cut downtime and training costs, which increases productivity at large. It thus dawns on merchants that systems are important if they perform well but also need solid support behind them to ensure minimum disruption to operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Growth Enablement and Speed"},{"type":"p","text":"The attention to the enablement of growth, 82%, and operational speed, 81%, is indicative of the quest of merchants to meet the demands of the present and support future growth and flexibility. Scalability and flexibility of solutions can accommodate growth in business and dynamic market demands that offer strategic differentiation. Knowing customer behavior relative to shopping and purchasing patterns is core to enhancing customer experience and comprises the roadmap to sales."},{"type":"p","text":"Strategic Decision-Making"},{"type":"p","text":"The results of the survey point out that strategic decision-making concerning technology investments essentially boils down to a balancing act between innovation and mitigating risks. Hence, leaders are looking for integrated, secure, and efficient systems that can drive growth not at the cost of jeopardizing operations. Providers capable of delivering integrated, secure, and complete solutions may best fit such needs."},{"type":"p","text":"Industry Implications"},{"type":"p","text":"These insights draw attention to the areas of opportunities and the key focus areas for hospitality technology providers. From the strategic point of view, promotion of integration abilities, fortification of security measures, betterment of user experience, and strong customer support are some of the significant steps toward gaining and retaining enterprise clients. It is in aligning product development with these priorities that providers have the scope to satisfy dynamic industry requirements with some degree of effectiveness."},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"The recent survey conducted by FreedomPay and Toast delivered important insight into security in data, integration, and enablement-driven growth at enterprise hospitality leaders. Providers of technologies should, therefore, focus on these key domains as a driver of solutions toward improved operational efficiency, increasing customer trust, and growing business. In this way, such technology providers will be aiding hospitality businesses to navigate the complexities of today''s commerce toward assured long-term success."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_5e694974229f47c5842dfe621bbb2773~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/103(27-june-blog-image).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-25', 'published'),
  ('nyc-restaurant-owners-brace-for-potential-43%-delivery-app-fees', 'NYC Restaurant Owners Brace for Potential 43% Delivery App Fees', 'Will NYC Restaurants Survive a 43% Delivery Commission Hike? Owners Fear the Impact of Proposed Bill', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Will NYC Restaurants Survive a 43% Delivery Commission Hike? Owners Fear the Impact of Proposed Bill"},{"type":"p","text":"The New York City Council is currently reviewing a bill, Int 762, that could significantly alter the financial landscape for restaurants utilizing third-party delivery apps. The proposed legislation would allow apps like DoorDash, Uber Eats, and Grubhub to charge total commissions of up to 43% per order, a considerable increase from the current 23% cap."},{"type":"p","text":"Marketing Fees at the Center of Debate"},{"type":"p","text":"The most significant change under the proposed bill would impact marketing fees, potentially raising the current 5% cap to a maximum of 25%. This increase would allow restaurants to purchase additional visibility on the apps, potentially boosting their reach and competitiveness. However, this has sparked concerns about the financial burden on smaller businesses and the possibility of those unable to afford the higher fees being overshadowed."},{"type":"p","text":"Differing Perspectives on the Bill"},{"type":"p","text":"Delivery apps have voiced support for the bill, highlighting the potential benefits for restaurants in terms of flexibility and growth opportunities. However, restaurant advocates like the New York City Hospitality Alliance have raised concerns about the bill''s potential negative impact on small businesses. They argue that the increased fees could unfairly burden smaller establishments and create an uneven playing field."},{"type":"p","text":"New York City: A Unique Landscape for Delivery Fees"},{"type":"p","text":"New York City currently stands alone as the only city in the United States with permanent restrictions on delivery app fees. The proposed 43% ceiling in the bill even exceeds the typical charges in other markets, where a tiered model maxing out at 30% is the norm. This makes the bill a pivotal point in the ongoing debate over fair compensation and the impact of delivery apps on local businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"The Path Forward"},{"type":"p","text":"The bill, currently sponsored by 20 of the city''s 51 Council members, requires 26 votes to pass. As it progresses through the legislative process, the outcome of this debate will undoubtedly shape the future relationship between restaurants and delivery apps in New York City."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_72a7191c9a264481bb9f582801f8fac5~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/98-(25-new-blog)%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-24', 'published'),
  ('pbna-strengthens-western-u.s.-presence-with-new-colorado-distribution-facility', 'PBNA Strengthens Western U.S. Presence with New Colorado Distribution Facility', 'PBNA Expands Footprint with State-of-the-Art Distribution Hub in Colorado, USA', '[{"type":"h2","text":"PBNA Expands Footprint with State-of-the-Art Distribution Hub in Colorado, USA"},{"type":"p","text":"PepsiCo Beverages North America (PBNA) recently unveiled a new 115,000-square-foot distribution center in Colorado Springs, significantly enhancing its distribution network and inventory capacity. This state-of-the-art facility allows PBNA to quadruple its previous capacity, ensuring efficient delivery of popular brands like Pepsi, Gatorade, Celsius, and Rockstar to consumers across Colorado and the broader US market."},{"type":"p","text":"Sustainable Design and Technology at the Forefront"},{"type":"p","text":"The Colorado Springs facility is a testament to PepsiCo''s commitment to sustainability. Equipped with solar panels to power delivery fleet pallet jacks, the facility is designed with a roof that can accommodate future solar expansion, reducing reliance on traditional energy sources. The implementation of LED motion-controlled lighting and an EV conduit installation further underscore the company''s dedication to minimizing its environmental impact."},{"type":"p","text":"Global Investments Strengthen PepsiCo''s Position"},{"type":"p","text":"This new facility is just one part of PepsiCo''s broader strategy to invest in its global infrastructure and enhance its distribution network. The company recently announced a $160 million investment in a new salty snacks plant in Kazakhstan, expanding its international presence. Additionally, PepsiCo invested £8 million in its Pipers Crisps manufacturing site in the UK and NR 12.66 billion (approx. $151.7 million) in a new flavor manufacturing facility in India, solidifying its position as a global leader in the food and beverage industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Commitment to Innovation and Sustainability"},{"type":"p","text":"By continually investing in cutting-edge facilities and sustainable technologies, PepsiCo demonstrates its commitment to innovation, efficiency, and responsible business practices. The Colorado Springs expansion exemplifies the company''s dedication to meeting growing consumer demand while minimizing its environmental footprint. This strategic move sets a new industry standard, showcasing PepsiCo''s leadership in both operational excellence and environmental stewardship."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_06464bcbf5cf439ba3f4e85586e68d4b~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(20).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-22', 'published'),
  ('new-york-bill-outlaws-black-market-for-restaurant-reservations', 'New York Bill Outlaws Black Market for Restaurant Reservations', 'NY Cracks Down on Reservation Resellers', '[{"type":"h2","text":"NY Cracks Down on Reservation Resellers"},{"type":"p","text":"In June, a bill was passed in New York that forbade the sale of reservations obtained via automated systems on Internet forums. We are awaiting the signature of Governor Kathy Hochul on the Restaurant Reservation Anti-Piracy Act."},{"type":"p","text":"Defying Predatory Software"},{"type":"p","text":"According to a press release, if she signs it, New York will spearhead national efforts to combat the \"trend of predatory software flooding the online restaurant reservation marketplace.\" Given that it already has what are arguably the most fierce reservation wars in the country, New York is well-positioned to be the first."},{"type":"p","text":"The Struggle for Prime Reservations"},{"type":"p","text":"Are you trying to get three people into Carbone on a Friday night at six o''clock? Never even bother. The emergence of reservation platforms in New York, such as Resy, Opentable, Tock, and SevenRooms, has turned the competition for available slots into a reality show. People naturally devised methods to game systems. In these forums, a lot of reservations are made by bots, so it was never really a war to wait until midnight for a restaurant to open for business for the month."},{"type":"p","text":"Creating a Culture of Exclusivity"},{"type":"p","text":"The bill''s supporters claim that it has created a culture in which the wealthy and destitute must pay hundreds of dollars simply to obtain a reservation, and that''s before the expensive meal bills at restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"Eater revealed in 2022 that finance bros created a closed online group chat on the encrypted messaging app Telegram called #FreeRezy, which included members of the Chainsmokers band as users. #FreeRezy was eventually discovered, but other groups have since taken its place. At the time, #FreeRezy told Eater, \"The benefit to someone in the group is you don''t have to plan a month.\""},{"type":"p","text":"\"People in their twenties lead hectic lives.\" Restaurants have also been left in the dark by untrustworthy reservations and a wave of cancellations from untrustworthy patrons. Many restaurants now charge no-show fees in its place."},{"type":"p","text":"Legitimate Reasons for the Black Market"},{"type":"p","text":"The black market may have grown for a few acceptable reasons: Following a positive COVID test, users on the Reddit group R/FoodNYC tried to hawk their nonrefundable, $1500 fine dining reservations during the omicron wave. The subReddit has continued to be used as a platform for reservation transfers in the years that have passed."},{"type":"p","text":"R/FoodNYC is primarily about discussions about food in New York, such as what to eat after the theater, so this was not its intended use. Eater receives a warning from a group moderator that anyone who upcharges on their non-refundable reservation trades risks being removed from the group."},{"type":"p","text":"Legislative Support and Industry Backing"},{"type":"p","text":"Applauded by the New York State Restaurant Association is bill S.9365/A.10215. \"New Yorkers should not have to pay shady middlemen just for the right to a dinner reservation,\" Assemblymember Alex Bores backed it as well. We are making sure that families won''t have to pay a $250, $500, or even $1,000 cover charge to celebrate a graduation, anniversary, or birthday thanks to this legislation."},{"type":"p","text":"We also shield workers from missing tips and restaurants from an increase in cancellations. genuinely win-win-win OpenTable and Resy are joining the chorus of supporters, which makes sense because it increases the relevance of their respective platforms in particular. The bill is \"a significant step forward to protect restaurants and diners from reservation fraud,\" according to Pablo Rivero, CEO of Resy."},{"type":"p","text":"Looking Ahead"},{"type":"p","text":"If enacted, this legislation may serve as a template for other states facing comparable challenges. It is a big step toward guaranteeing equitable access to reservations for dining and shielding customers and the restaurant business from dishonest business practices. A testament to New York''s dedication to preserving the integrity of its thriving dining scene is the Restaurant Reservation Anti-Piracy Act."},{"type":"p","text":"As evidence of its dedication to maintaining justice and openness in the restaurant business, New York has established a precedent in the fight against reservation fraud. In addition to safeguarding customers, this law creates a more reliable and long-lasting atmosphere that is conducive to restaurant success. This legislation could have a nationwide effect, changing reservation procedures and ensuring that everyone has a safe and enjoyable dining experience as other states take notice and may even implement comparable legislation."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_b42b9e1136644d67af32baa470843626~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/blxk%20marejt.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-21', 'published'),
  ('ready,-set,-nominate!-2024-automation-&-self-service-awards-are-calling', 'Ready, Set, Nominate! 2024 Automation & Self-Service Awards are Calling', 'Deadline Approaching: Submit Your Groundbreaking Solutions Today!', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Deadline Approaching: Submit Your Groundbreaking Solutions Today!"},{"type":"p","text":"Hey there, tech trailblazers and automation aficionados! The time has come to put a spotlight on the game-changers who are revolutionizing how we interact with technology and services. Nominations for the 2024 Automation & Self-Service Awards are in full swing, and it''s an event you won''t want to miss."},{"type":"p","text":"Why These Awards Matter"},{"type":"p","text":"Picture this: a world where your daily tasks are streamlined, your customer experiences are seamless, and your business operations are humming with efficiency. That''s the future that automation and self-service are building, and these awards celebrate the companies and individuals at the forefront of that movement."},{"type":"p","text":"These aren''t your average awards - they''re a recognition of ingenuity, a platform for knowledge sharing, and a celebration of the endless possibilities that technology holds. By participating, you''re not just vying for a shiny trophy; you''re joining a community of innovators who are shaping the way we live and work."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Ticket to Recognition and Inspiration"},{"type":"p","text":"Whether you''re a nimble startup or an industry titan, these awards are designed to showcase your accomplishments. Imagine the buzz generated when your groundbreaking solution takes center stage, attracting the attention of potential customers, investors, and partners."},{"type":"p","text":"Beyond the prestige, the awards ceremony at the Self-Service Innovation Summit in Tampa is a prime opportunity for networking. Rub shoulders with industry leaders, exchange ideas with fellow innovators, and gain insights that can propel your business to new heights."},{"type":"p","text":"But it''s not all about the glitz and glamour. The Automation & Self-Service Awards are also a source of inspiration. By showcasing real-world applications of automation and self-service, we can spark new ideas, ignite conversations, and encourage even greater innovation across industries."},{"type":"p","text":"The Path to Nomination: Easy as 1, 2, 3"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Check Your Calendar: Ensure your project was completed after October 1, 2023."},{"type":"p","text":"2. Choose Your Categories: Decide which of the six categories best align with your innovation (you can enter multiple categories)."},{"type":"p","text":"3. Submit by September 6th: Complete the nomination form with a $200 fee per category (except for the \"Influencer of the Year\" category, which is free)."},{"type":"p","text":"The Categories: Where Your Innovation Shines"},{"type":"ul","items":["Best Vending Solution: Did you create a vending machine that''s more than just a snack dispenser? If it''s interactive, efficient, and user-friendly, this is your category.","Best Kiosk Solution: Have you designed a kiosk that elevates the customer experience, whether it''s for ordering, information access, or payments? This is where it belongs.","Best Use of Robotics: Are robots the stars of your show? If they''re performing tasks with precision and improving efficiency, this is their moment to shine.","Best Use of AI: Is artificial intelligence the brains behind your operation? If it''s powering smart interactions, data analysis, or customer service, let''s see it in action.","Responsible Innovation Award: Does your solution not only solve problems but also address social responsibility concerns like sustainability, accessibility, and inclusivity? This award is for you.","Influencer of the Year: Know someone who''s a driving force in the automation and self-service space? Nominate this trailblazer (for free!) and give them the recognition they deserve."]},{"type":"p","text":"The Countdown Begins"},{"type":"p","text":"The clock is ticking, innovators! Don''t miss your chance to be part of this celebration of ingenuity and progress. Click here today and share your story with the world. We can''t wait to see the incredible ways you''re shaping the future of automation and self-service."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_eb235d3c2d25421a8d35c54815aadc7c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Industry%20News%20June%2020.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-20', 'published');
